        <section ids="bug" names="bug">
            <title>Bug</title>
            <bullet_list bullet="*">
                <list_item>
                    <paragraph>Fix parsing of connections where variables have the same name in different components by <reference name="@hsorby" refuri="https://github.com/hsorby">@hsorby</reference><target ids="hsorby" names="@hsorby" refuri="https://github.com/hsorby"></target> [<reference name="#1500" refuri="https://github.com/cellml/libcellml/pull/1500">#1500</reference><target ids="id1" names="#1500" refuri="https://github.com/cellml/libcellml/pull/1500"></target>].</paragraph>
                </list_item>
                <list_item>
                    <paragraph>Units: a reference to imported units keeps its exponent by <reference name="@FinbarArgus" refuri="https://github.com/FinbarArgus">@FinbarArgus</reference><target ids="finbarargus" names="@finbarargus" refuri="https://github.com/FinbarArgus"></target> [<reference name="#1498" refuri="https://github.com/cellml/libcellml/pull/1498">#1498</reference><target ids="id2" names="#1498" refuri="https://github.com/cellml/libcellml/pull/1498"></target>].</paragraph>
                </list_item>
                <list_item>
                    <paragraph>Analyser unit check raises the multiplier of a unit to its exponent, in contrast to the specification and Units::scalingFactor by <reference name="@agarny" refuri="https://github.com/agarny">@agarny</reference><target ids="agarny" names="@agarny" refuri="https://github.com/agarny"></target> [<reference name="#1467" refuri="https://github.com/cellml/libcellml/pull/1467">#1467</reference><target ids="id3" names="#1467" refuri="https://github.com/cellml/libcellml/pull/1467"></target>].</paragraph>
